Context marker: INTERVIEW-112-01546a28a94c5422.

Replace `src/core.mjs` with:
```js
export function solve(n, edges, source) {
  const d = Array(n).fill(Infinity);
  const q = [[0, source]];
  d[source] = 0;

  while (q.length) {
    q.sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0]);
    const [c, u] = q.shift();
    if (c !== d[u]) continue;

    for (const [a, b, w] of edges) {
      if (a !== u) continue;
      const candidate = c + w;
      if (candidate < d[b]) {
        d[b] = candidate;
        q.push([candidate, b]);
      }
    }
  }

  return d.map(x => Number.isFinite(x) ? x : null);
}
```

The restored invariant is that each distance is the best route discovered so far, and every strict improvement enters the queue. With nonnegative weights, processing the smallest current distance makes it final; stale queue entries are skipped rather than blocking improvements at discovery. Parallel edges and zero-weight edges now work correctly, while unreachable vertices remain `null`; the synchronous API is unchanged.

